From: Justin Walsh <contact.me@thejustinwalsh.com>
Date: Sun, 27 Sep 2026 20:30:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] server: the tiered-KV draft tail keys on pool cells, not the slot position

The series' 0031 drafts --spec-draft-n-max-tail once a slot's POSITION
reaches --kv-vram-cells. The VRAM line of 0028 is on CELLS: cells [0, N)
of each layer's K/V are in VRAM. With one slot a position and a cell
count agree; with a unified pool (-np > 1) they do not: every sequence's
attention spans n_kv = pad(used_max_p1) cells of the one stream, so the
host tail is read by EVERY slot as soon as ANY slot's cells reach it, and
by none before, whatever the slot's own depth.

New: llama_memory_cells_used_max_p1() (llama_kv_cache: the max of
v_cells[s].used_max_p1() over streams, the quantity get_n_kv() pads;
hybrid memory: its attention cache; any other memory: 0), and the server
drafts the tail size while that exceeds --kv-vram-cells. Tail drafting
only; nothing about what is stored or computed changes.
---
diff --git a/include/llama.h b/include/llama.h
index 555ff32dc..f228f449a 100644
--- a/include/llama.h
+++ b/include/llama.h
@@ -813,6 +813,10 @@ extern "C" {
             llama_memory_t mem,
               llama_seq_id seq_id);
 
+    // One past the highest KV cell in use (0 if none): an attention op spans the cells below it, so a tiered
+    // cache (--kv-vram-cells N) reads its host tail exactly when this exceeds N, for every sequence of the pool
+    LLAMA_API uint32_t llama_memory_cells_used_max_p1(llama_memory_t mem);
+
     // Check if the memory supports shifting
     LLAMA_API bool llama_memory_can_shift(llama_memory_t mem);
 
diff --git a/src/llama-context.cpp b/src/llama-context.cpp
index 6daf5c674..0d79c1e5d 100644
--- a/src/llama-context.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-context.cpp
@@ -4320,6 +4320,14 @@ llama_pos llama_memory_seq_pos_max(
     return mem->seq_pos_max(seq_id);
 }
 
+uint32_t llama_memory_cells_used_max_p1(llama_memory_t mem) {
+    if (!mem) {
+        return 0;
+    }
+
+    return mem->cells_used_max_p1();
+}
+
 bool llama_memory_can_shift(llama_memory_t mem) {
     if (!mem) {
         return false;
diff --git a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
index 723737acb..108d9533b 100644
--- a/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-kv-cache.cpp
@@ -715,6 +715,21 @@ llama_pos llama_kv_cache::seq_pos_max(llama_seq_id seq_id) const {
     return cells.seq_pos_max(seq_id);
 }
 
+uint32_t llama_kv_cache::cells_used_max_p1() const {
+    // TODO: refactor [TAG_KV_CACHE_SHARE_CELLS]
+    if (other) {
+        return other->cells_used_max_p1();
+    }
+
+    // the same quantity get_n_kv() pads into n_kv, over every stream
+    uint32_t result = 0;
+    for (const auto & cells : v_cells) {
+        result = std::max(result, cells.used_max_p1());
+    }
+
+    return result;
+}
+
